# Git: integrate on `main`

`main` is the only integration branch. New work never lands as direct development commits on `main`.

- Create a branch or `git worktree` from current `main` (or `origin/main`) before implementing.
- When the change is complete, merge into `main` with `git merge --no-ff` so the feature commits stay in history.
- Do not squash-merge, rewrite `main`, or force-push `main`.
- Keep unrelated uncommitted or in-progress branch work out of the merge.